{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3061","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3061","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3061\",\"parent_revision\":\"c5ed3eadaf949f60ceffeaa7fd589db0ed20b5bb23105c11106ff6fa8e28802a\",\"root_revision\":\"c5ed3eadaf949f60ceffeaa7fd589db0ed20b5bb23105c11106ff6fa8e28802a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nSections and artifacts are separate namespaces with separate lookups. An agent viewing an item receives sections but must call a different tool to discover which reports and artifacts exist for it.\\n\\nR6 requires both in one response, each requestable by name. This changes the item-view response shape on every transport.\\n\\nOwnership per the component map: registration, identity, and item association belong to the backlog package; durability belongs to the storage provider; delivery of content belongs to the markdown engine.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] One item-view response carries both the section table of contents and the artifact inventory\\n- [ ] Both are requestable by name from that response\\n- [ ] Discovering what exists for an item requires no second call to a different tool\\n- [ ] Behaviour is identical across transports\\n- [ ] The combined inventory paginates when large, per R2\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- Blocked by #3055 \u2014 artifact content retrieval must be reliable before the inventory moves onto the default read path\\n- Intended behaviour is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`. Component ownership is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/component-architecture.md`. Parent: #3054.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"87ab438d036b4b464ed8120d2408876fb4a78862b3eefdd3d8da74200f375be9\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPvbvng\"}"}